# The repo standard is LF on every text file: TypeScript, Rust, JSON,
# Markdown, YAML, TOML, CSS, HTML. This file is the answer to where CRLF kept
# coming from: machines running git with core.autocrlf=true convert checked
# out files to CRLF, and without this file nothing in the repository says
# otherwise. Declared attributes take precedence over core.autocrlf, so this
# pins the checkout and checkin endings for every machine that clones it.
# The one-time cleanup of the files already committed with CRLF is a
# renormalize pass, deliberately not done as part of the audit that found
# them; see report/CLEANUP-what-seven-phases-left-behind.md for the measured
# list.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, named rather than trusted to auto-detection.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary
*.node binary
*.wasm binary
"STUDIO HARNESS/vendor/**" binary
